WEBVTT

00:00:09.879 --> 00:00:11.141
[grunts]

00:00:13.926 --> 00:00:14.840
Hey.

00:00:15.015 --> 00:00:16.538
Fixing yourself a snack?

00:00:16.712 --> 00:00:18.757
Oh, I thought
I'd clean up a little.

00:00:18.931 --> 00:00:20.585
Noticed we made
a bit of a mess yesterday.

00:00:20.759 --> 00:00:22.805
-Oh. No.
-[flies buzzing]

00:00:22.979 --> 00:00:24.850
I hadn't noticed.

00:00:25.025 --> 00:00:27.288
Um, you can just put that
over there in the compost bin.

00:00:27.462 --> 00:00:28.506
Oh!

00:00:28.680 --> 00:00:30.552
-Smart.
-[clunking]

00:00:30.726 --> 00:00:31.944
[shouts]

00:00:32.902 --> 00:00:34.469
Good job.

00:00:34.643 --> 00:00:35.818
Well, we didn't want you
to think

00:00:35.992 --> 00:00:37.385
we're a family of savages.

00:00:37.559 --> 00:00:39.735
-[chuckles]
-[trumpeting]

00:00:39.909 --> 00:00:41.563
[laughs]
Savages.

00:00:41.737 --> 00:00:44.000
Sandy, drop it.

00:00:44.174 --> 00:00:46.002
-Drop it!
-[screeches]

00:00:46.176 --> 00:00:47.743
Kids, right?
[chuckles]

00:00:47.917 --> 00:00:49.397
[clears throat]
So, Ugga,

00:00:49.571 --> 00:00:51.225
you must really miss the wild.

00:00:51.399 --> 00:00:52.878
Right?
With the hunting...

00:00:53.053 --> 00:00:54.837
-Not really.
-...and the gathering and...

00:00:55.011 --> 00:00:55.925
Not really.

00:00:56.099 --> 00:00:57.796
...the baying at the moon.

00:00:57.970 --> 00:00:59.233
[howling]

00:00:59.407 --> 00:01:00.799
Not at all.

00:01:00.973 --> 00:01:03.498
Honestly, it sucks out there.

00:01:03.672 --> 00:01:06.501
If no one's died
before breakfast, it's a win.

00:01:06.675 --> 00:01:10.157
[chuckles]
It is so much better in here.

00:01:10.331 --> 00:01:11.506
Oh.

00:01:11.680 --> 00:01:12.681
That's nice.

00:01:12.855 --> 00:01:13.682
[creaking]

00:01:13.856 --> 00:01:15.510
Yeah.

00:01:15.684 --> 00:01:18.469
Actually, Grug and I
were thinking that maybe we...

00:01:18.643 --> 00:01:20.602
Ah. I almost forgot.

00:01:20.776 --> 00:01:23.170
-I made this for you.
-A basket?

00:01:23.344 --> 00:01:26.738
Mm-hmm. Well, it's more
like a-- like a travel basket.

00:01:26.912 --> 00:01:28.088
Travel basket?

00:01:28.262 --> 00:01:29.524
Yeah. For the road.

00:01:29.698 --> 00:01:31.569
It's got fruit, nuts, soap,

00:01:31.743 --> 00:01:34.311
more soap and a neck pillow.

00:01:34.485 --> 00:01:36.139
Oh. Yeah.

00:01:36.313 --> 00:01:37.445
This'll be great.

00:01:37.619 --> 00:01:39.186
For the road.

00:01:39.360 --> 00:01:40.665
Thank you.

00:01:40.839 --> 00:01:42.319
It's the least we can do
to thank you

00:01:42.493 --> 00:01:43.712
for bringing Guy home.

00:01:43.886 --> 00:01:45.061
-Home?
-Home.

00:01:45.235 --> 00:01:46.149
Guy?

00:01:46.323 --> 00:01:47.585
Guy's home. You got it.

00:01:47.759 --> 00:01:50.022
Well, got to go.
See you at dinner, 'kay?

00:01:50.197 --> 00:01:51.937
[basket creaking]

00:01:52.112 --> 00:01:53.113
[grunts]

00:01:55.071 --> 00:01:57.073
[whooping]

00:01:57.247 --> 00:01:58.205
Yeah!

00:01:58.379 --> 00:02:01.077
-[whooping]
-[snarling]

00:02:01.251 --> 00:02:02.296
[laughs]

00:02:02.470 --> 00:02:04.298
Ooh.

00:02:04.472 --> 00:02:06.256
Huh? Whoa!

00:02:08.345 --> 00:02:09.172
[chuckling]:
Whoa.

00:02:09.346 --> 00:02:11.696
[laughing]

00:02:11.870 --> 00:02:14.656
-[laughing]: Yeah!
-[whooping]

00:02:14.830 --> 00:02:16.875
♪ ♪

00:02:22.316 --> 00:02:24.187
-[gasps]
-Whoa!

00:02:24.361 --> 00:02:26.363
[trilling]

00:02:30.541 --> 00:02:32.543
[laughing]

00:02:35.938 --> 00:02:37.679
Ooh!

00:02:37.853 --> 00:02:39.768
-[laughing]
-Huh?

00:02:39.942 --> 00:02:40.986
Eep!

00:02:43.075 --> 00:02:43.989
[grunting]

00:02:44.164 --> 00:02:45.513
-Eep?
-[groaning]

00:02:45.687 --> 00:02:47.167
-[screaming]
-[buzzing]

00:02:47.341 --> 00:02:48.385
[surprised snarling]

00:02:48.559 --> 00:02:49.952
-[grunting]
-[buzzing]

00:02:50.126 --> 00:02:51.910
[groans]

00:02:52.084 --> 00:02:55.349
[grunting]

00:02:56.480 --> 00:02:58.308
-[muffled growl]
-[laughing]

00:02:58.482 --> 00:02:59.701
[laughs]

00:02:59.875 --> 00:03:00.702
[gasping]

00:03:00.876 --> 00:03:02.486
[buzzing]

00:03:02.660 --> 00:03:04.096
Ow.

00:03:04.271 --> 00:03:06.186
I have a scar.

00:03:06.360 --> 00:03:07.535
You have a scar!

00:03:07.709 --> 00:03:09.145
-I have a scar!
-Yeah!

00:03:09.319 --> 00:03:10.407
Ow!

00:03:10.581 --> 00:03:12.801
[steam hissing]

00:03:12.975 --> 00:03:14.411
[Phil sighs]

00:03:14.585 --> 00:03:16.108
Don't tell Mrs. Betterman,

00:03:16.283 --> 00:03:19.590
but while she thinks
I'm toiling in the hot sun,

00:03:19.764 --> 00:03:21.505
I'm actually in here,

00:03:21.679 --> 00:03:23.768
my man cave.

00:03:23.942 --> 00:03:24.900
Whew.

00:03:25.074 --> 00:03:26.989
It's hot in here.

00:03:27.163 --> 00:03:28.643
Grug, you might be
more comfortable

00:03:28.817 --> 00:03:30.993
if you removed your fur pelt.

00:03:31.167 --> 00:03:32.647
I-I already did.

00:03:32.821 --> 00:03:34.170
Right.

00:03:34.344 --> 00:03:36.303
Yeah, it's a place
a father can escape

00:03:36.477 --> 00:03:38.392
the chaos of family life.

00:03:38.566 --> 00:03:41.003
Relax, hang with his bros,

00:03:41.177 --> 00:03:43.484
if bros he has.

00:03:43.658 --> 00:03:44.485
Another shark milk?

00:03:44.659 --> 00:03:45.964
So,

00:03:46.138 --> 00:03:49.794
y-you come in here
to hide from your family?

00:03:49.968 --> 00:03:51.927
Not hide. Help.

00:03:52.101 --> 00:03:54.321
I help my family.
[slurps]

00:03:54.495 --> 00:03:56.148
[sighs]

00:03:57.106 --> 00:03:58.890
So...

00:03:59.064 --> 00:04:00.109
uh...

00:04:00.283 --> 00:04:01.763
how does this help your family?

00:04:01.937 --> 00:04:03.155
Yeah. [grunts]

00:04:03.330 --> 00:04:05.375
This is where I find solutions

00:04:05.549 --> 00:04:07.290
to my family's biggest problems.

00:04:07.464 --> 00:04:09.292
[steam hissing]

00:04:09.466 --> 00:04:10.293
Okay.

00:04:10.467 --> 00:04:12.687
So, feeling relaxed?

00:04:12.861 --> 00:04:13.949
Comfortable?

00:04:14.123 --> 00:04:16.995
Susceptible to suggestion?

00:04:18.345 --> 00:04:19.911
What's your problem, big guy?

00:04:20.085 --> 00:04:21.739
Uh... I don't have a problem.

00:04:21.913 --> 00:04:23.045
Come on, Grug.

00:04:23.219 --> 00:04:24.612
I've seen you moping around.

00:04:24.786 --> 00:04:25.700
What's your problem?

00:04:25.874 --> 00:04:26.788
I'm hot.

00:04:26.962 --> 00:04:28.093
That's-that's my problem.

00:04:28.268 --> 00:04:29.225
Knock, knock.

00:04:29.399 --> 00:04:31.096
I'm knocking on the door,
big guy.

00:04:31.271 --> 00:04:32.576
Open it.

00:04:32.750 --> 00:04:33.751
[sighs] No.

00:04:35.275 --> 00:04:36.101
Open up to me.

00:04:36.276 --> 00:04:37.581
-No.
-Share with me.

00:04:37.755 --> 00:04:38.887
Uh-uh. I don't wanna.

00:04:39.061 --> 00:04:40.192
I'm-I'm hot.

00:04:40.367 --> 00:04:41.281
PHIL:
Tell me your problem.

00:04:41.455 --> 00:04:42.804
I don't have a problem.

00:04:42.978 --> 00:04:44.371
You have a problem.

00:04:44.545 --> 00:04:46.373
[echoing]:
Tell me your problem.

00:04:47.548 --> 00:04:49.027
-I don't-- I don't...
-Tell me. Tell me.

00:04:49.201 --> 00:04:50.725
-I don't...
-Tell me. Tell me. Tell me.

00:04:50.899 --> 00:04:52.596
I don't like it here,
all right?!

00:04:52.770 --> 00:04:53.989
[crying]:
My pack's all split up.

00:04:54.163 --> 00:04:55.469
There's no one
to sleep-pile with.

00:04:55.643 --> 00:04:57.384
You won't let me eat bananas.

00:04:57.558 --> 00:04:58.994
Guy gave Eep a rock.
[sniffles]

00:04:59.168 --> 00:05:00.517
He kissed my hand.

00:05:00.691 --> 00:05:02.606
They're planning
on leaving the pack.

00:05:02.780 --> 00:05:04.216
And I don't like you at all!

00:05:04.391 --> 00:05:06.567
Hmm. Now, that's interesting.

00:05:06.741 --> 00:05:09.700
You know, maybe I just need
to get to know you better.

00:05:09.874 --> 00:05:10.745
No, not that.

00:05:10.919 --> 00:05:12.224
The part about Eep and Guy.

00:05:12.399 --> 00:05:15.967
Oh. Guy's trying
to take my daughter away.

00:05:16.141 --> 00:05:18.970
Father to father,
I worry about my daughter, too.

00:05:19.144 --> 00:05:22.539
-She was so lonely
before Guy came back. -Yeah.

00:05:22.713 --> 00:05:25.803
It's almost like...
Guy's the problem.

00:05:25.977 --> 00:05:27.327
Wait a minute.

00:05:27.501 --> 00:05:29.198
Are you saying
what I think you're saying?

00:05:29.372 --> 00:05:31.156
Yes. No.

00:05:31.331 --> 00:05:32.157
I don't know.

00:05:32.332 --> 00:05:34.508
-Hot.
-Are you suggesting...

00:05:34.682 --> 00:05:36.292
we take Guy off your hands...

00:05:36.466 --> 00:05:37.902
so Dawn isn't lonely...

00:05:38.076 --> 00:05:39.817
and Eep stays with you...

00:05:39.991 --> 00:05:41.732
with your pack?

00:05:41.906 --> 00:05:44.126
Uh... am I?

00:05:44.300 --> 00:05:46.868
Why, Grug,
that's a truly great idea.

00:05:47.042 --> 00:05:48.086
You've done it!

00:05:48.260 --> 00:05:49.827
You've solved both our problems!

00:05:50.001 --> 00:05:51.786
[scoffing chuckle]
No.

00:05:51.960 --> 00:05:52.961
Really?

00:05:53.135 --> 00:05:54.789
So, we have a deal... bro?

00:05:55.964 --> 00:05:57.531
GRUG:
Deal.

00:06:00.272 --> 00:06:02.579
[footsteps approaching]

00:06:02.753 --> 00:06:04.102
[chuckles]:
Hey, Ugga.

00:06:04.276 --> 00:06:06.496
I just had the best time
with Phil. Look at me.

00:06:06.670 --> 00:06:09.151
Standing up straight,
got lots of ideas.

00:06:09.325 --> 00:06:10.805
You know,
Phil's a good listener.

00:06:10.979 --> 00:06:14.591
He knows a smart idea
when he hears one.

00:06:17.202 --> 00:06:18.552
[chuckles]

00:06:18.726 --> 00:06:21.598
[sighs]
The Bettermans want us to leave

00:06:21.772 --> 00:06:23.557
-without Guy.
-Oh. Um...

00:06:23.731 --> 00:06:25.863
-You think so, huh?
-As if we would ever do that.

00:06:26.037 --> 00:06:28.039
-Well...
-Guy's a member of our pack.

00:06:28.213 --> 00:06:30.433
-Kinda. -And can you imagine
what that would do to Eep?

00:06:30.607 --> 00:06:32.261
It would absolutely destroy her.

00:06:32.435 --> 00:06:34.045
Well, initially.

00:06:34.219 --> 00:06:35.830
They think we're just
simple cave people,

00:06:36.004 --> 00:06:37.266
that we're so stupid,

00:06:37.440 --> 00:06:39.399
we'd trade Guy
for a fruit basket.

00:06:39.573 --> 00:06:43.054
And then she tried to make me
think it was my idea!

00:06:43.228 --> 00:06:46.057
-That is a great idea.
-Betterman.

00:06:46.231 --> 00:06:48.103
UGGA:
As if we'd ever do that.

00:06:48.277 --> 00:06:50.453
-So, we have a deal?
-Betterman.

00:06:50.627 --> 00:06:52.499
UGGA: They must think
we're pretty stupid.

00:06:52.673 --> 00:06:54.326
You've done it, Grug.
Thinking man.

00:06:54.501 --> 00:06:56.633
-You're not stupid.
-Betterman!

00:06:56.807 --> 00:06:58.983
-Betterman.
-Betterman!

00:06:59.157 --> 00:07:00.463
Betterman!

00:07:00.637 --> 00:07:01.595
[grunts]

00:07:01.769 --> 00:07:03.074
Betterman!

00:07:03.248 --> 00:07:04.598
[yelling]

00:07:06.948 --> 00:07:08.123
Maybe we should
take it down a notch, honey.

00:07:08.297 --> 00:07:09.429
Buhr-brah-brah?

00:07:09.603 --> 00:07:11.300
Buhr-brah-brah.
We got to focus.

00:07:11.474 --> 00:07:13.911
We've got to get Guy
and get out of here.

00:07:14.085 --> 00:07:15.870
Okay. But first,

00:07:16.044 --> 00:07:17.349
there's something
I've wanted to do

00:07:17.524 --> 00:07:20.396
for a really, really long time.

